{"name":"Innocent Snowdrop","hex":"#d0c7ff","fetched":"2026-10-16","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"innocent","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["Free from guilt, sin, or immorality.","Bearing no legal responsibility for a wrongful act."]},{"part":"Noun","definitions":["One who is innocent, especially a young child.","A harmless simple-minded person; an idiot."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/innocent"},{"term":"snowdrop","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["Any of the 20 species of the genus Galanthus of the Amaryllidaceae, bulbous flowering plants, bearing a solitary, pendulous, white, bell-shaped flower that appears, depending on species, between autumn and late winter or early spring, all native to temperate Eurasia.","Alternative letter-case form of Snowdrop (“a Royal Air Force police officer”)."]},{"part":"Verb","definitions":["To steal clothing (especially women's underwear) from a clothesline."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/snowdrop"}],"entries":[{"title":"Galanthus","blocks":[{"text":"Galanthus, or snowdrop, is a small genus of approximately 20 species of bulbous perennial herbaceous plants in the family Amaryllidaceae. The plants have two linear leaves and a single small white drooping bell-shaped flower with six petal-like (petaloid) tepals in two circles (whorls). The smaller inner petals have green markings."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/2/23/Galanthus_nivalis.jpg/330px-Galanthus_nivalis.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Galanthus"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/2/23/Galanthus_nivalis.jpg/500px-Galanthus_nivalis.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/2/23/Galanthus_nivalis.jpg/500px-Galanthus_nivalis.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign